[38;2;124;124;124mA locally ringed space (LRS) is a topological space with a sheaf of rings whose [0m[38;2;124;124;124mstalks are local rings. A locally ringed topos generalizes this: a topos [0m
[38;2;124;124;124m(category of sheaves) with a ring object whose stalks (in the appropriate sense)[0m[38;2;124;124;124mare local rings.[0m

[38;2;124;124;124mThe "strictly" condition: In a topos, the notion of "local ring" can be defined [0m[38;2;124;124;124minternally. A ring R in a topos is a "local ring object" if it satisfies the [0m
